{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","title":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2862,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","line":4877,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Smoothness of the Gram--Schmidt Frame]\n\\label{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth}\n\n\\uses{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth, lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth, lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth, lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators, def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame}\n\n\n\n\nEach normalized section $E_j$ is smooth on $u$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth,lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth,lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth,lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators}\n\\sketch The function $q_j(x)=g_x(U_j|_x,U_j|_x)$ is smooth and nowhere zero.\nLemma \\ref{lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth} makes $|q_j|^{-1/2}$ smooth, and\n$E_j=|q_j|^{-1/2}U_j$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Smoothness of the Gram--Schmidt Frame] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a70736575646f2d6772616d2d7363686d6964742d6672616d652d736d6f6f7468\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Apseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth\">↗ prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainv-sqrt-abs-smooth\">↗ lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apseudo-metric-pairing-smooth\">↗ lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators\">↗ lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apseudo-gram-schmidt-frame\">↗ def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame</a> <p></p>Each normalized section <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E_j$\">$E_j$</span> is smooth on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u$\">$u$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Apseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth\">↗ prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainv-sqrt-abs-smooth\">↗ lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apseudo-metric-pairing-smooth\">↗ lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators\">↗ lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators</a> \\sketch The function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_j(x)=g_x(U_j|_x,U_j|_x)$\">$q_j(x)=g_x(U_j|_x,U_j|_x)$</span> is smooth and nowhere zero. Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainv-sqrt-abs-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a696e762d737172742d6162732d736d6f6f7468\">16.2</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|q_j|^{-1/2}$\">$|q_j|^{-1/2}$</span> smooth, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E_j=|q_j|^{-1/2}U_j$\">$E_j=|q_j|^{-1/2}U_j$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-tuple-gram-matrix","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth","title":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth","label":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth","title":"lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth","label":"lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","title":"lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","label":"lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators","title":"lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators","label":"lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame","title":"def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame","label":"def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:orthonormalize-nondegenerate-family","title":"prop:orthonormalize-nondegenerate-family","label":"prop:orthonormalize-nondegenerate-family"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","title":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Smoothness of the Gram--Schmidt Frame]\n\\label{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-smooth}\n\n\\uses{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth, lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth, lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth, lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators, def:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame}\n\n\n\n\nEach normalized section $E_j$ is smooth on $u$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth,lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth,lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth,lem:pseudo-gram-schmidt-denominators}\n\\sketch The function $q_j(x)=g_x(U_j|_x,U_j|_x)$ is smooth and nowhere zero.\nLemma \\ref{lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth} makes $|q_j|^{-1/2}$ smooth, and\n$E_j=|q_j|^{-1/2}U_j$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth","title":"prop:pseudo-gram-schmidt-frame-aux-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth","title":"lem:inv-sqrt-abs-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","title":"lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ps